00:57:03,652 --> 00:57:08,632
Understanding question-answer relationships provides a basis for three comprehension strategies.

551
00:57:08,871 --> 00:57:10,652
Locating information, okay?

552
00:57:10,652 --> 00:57:15,532
So when a question is asked to you, if you know question-answer relationships,

553
00:57:15,532 --> 00:57:20,351
if you know how to identify the question type and how to look for it,

554
00:57:20,351 --> 00:57:24,032
then you can easily locate the information in the text.

555
00:57:24,172 --> 00:57:28,012
You can easily find the necessary information in the text.

556
00:57:30,412 --> 00:57:34,692
Again, showing text structures and textual organization,

557
00:57:34,692 --> 00:57:41,112
and determining when an inference or reading between the lines is required, okay?

558
00:57:41,632 --> 00:57:48,911
And in this way, you can identify how to categorize different types and levels of questions,

559
00:57:49,572 --> 00:57:52,672
as well as how the text does not have all the answers.

560
00:57:53,072 --> 00:57:57,371
Again, as I said, sometimes texts do not give all the answers necessary,

561
00:57:57,371 --> 00:58:01,351
but you draw conclusions, you infer information,

562
00:58:01,351 --> 00:58:06,432
or you understand some points when reading the points given in the text.

563
00:58:06,432 --> 00:58:15,271
And it also helps you consider both information from the text and information from your own background knowledge.

564
00:58:16,231 --> 00:58:20,851
And you will be able to think about the text and beyond it.

565
00:58:21,811 --> 00:58:25,632
It inspires you to think creatively and work cooperatively,

566
00:58:25,632 --> 00:58:30,032
while challenging you to use literal and higher level thinking skills.

567
00:58:30,032 --> 00:58:33,992
And in this way, when you understand question-answer relationships,

568
00:58:34,331 --> 00:58:40,192
you will extend your writing ability if you are asked to create your own questions, okay?

