00:58:44,472 --> 00:58:46,851
We can talk about three main categories.

571
00:58:47,152 --> 00:58:48,932
One is write-there questions.

572
00:58:49,251 --> 00:58:50,172
What does it mean?

573
00:58:50,731 --> 00:58:55,311
Write-there questions are questions that ask you to go to the text,

574
00:58:55,311 --> 00:58:59,672
go to a certain point of the text, a certain paragraph of the text,

575
00:58:59,672 --> 00:59:04,452
and get the information, find the information and give the answer, okay?

576
00:59:04,632 --> 00:59:07,351
So we call these questions write-there questions.

577
00:59:07,912 --> 00:59:10,532
The second category is think-and-search questions.

578
00:59:11,291 --> 00:59:16,532
Answers are given in the text, but they might be scattered to different parts of the text.

579
00:59:16,532 --> 00:59:20,771
So you read one, two, three parts of the text, different parts of the text,

580
00:59:20,771 --> 00:59:24,472
and you combine information you get from them.

581
00:59:25,811 --> 00:59:28,592
So you both think and you search for questions,

582
00:59:28,592 --> 00:59:31,172
and then you produce an answer.

583
00:59:31,952 --> 00:59:35,092
The third category might be author and you.

584
00:59:35,472 --> 00:59:36,391
What does it mean?

585
00:59:36,452 --> 00:59:40,432
The author, the text, gives you some piece of information,

586
00:59:40,432 --> 00:59:44,072
but to be able to answer a question about it,

587
00:59:44,112 --> 00:59:46,932
you need to use your own background information

588
00:59:46,932 --> 00:59:52,311
or your own reasoning skills to be able to answer the question, okay?

589
00:59:52,311 --> 00:59:56,192
So these are generally called inference questions, all right?

