01:01:14,771 --> 01:01:18,112
When skimming a text, you just have a general look at the text.

601
01:01:18,211 --> 01:01:20,692
But when scanning a text, you read it in detail.

602
01:01:21,052 --> 01:01:25,172
Okay, so you read again, you scan the text and look for keywords.

603
01:01:25,392 --> 01:01:30,412
These are the strategies that you can use to answer right there questions.

604
01:01:30,412 --> 01:01:35,392
For think and search questions, you can use skimming strategies.

605
01:01:35,592 --> 01:01:37,812
Again, you can use rereading strategies.

606
01:01:38,432 --> 01:01:43,912
You look for important information and you piece together different parts from the text.

607
01:01:44,592 --> 01:01:50,392
For author and me questions, again, you reread, you predict, you make some predictions.

608
01:01:50,392 --> 01:01:59,432
You try to understand what the piece of information leads to, where the piece of information leads you.

609
01:02:00,412 --> 01:02:07,372
Infer, as I said, infer means to draw conclusions, to understand from a text.

610
01:02:08,032 --> 01:02:11,771
And link what you already know and what the text says.

611
01:02:12,132 --> 01:02:12,312
Okay.

612
01:02:12,932 --> 01:02:21,251
So these are the basic question types and some strategies to use when looking for the answers.

613
01:02:22,711 --> 01:02:24,472
Any questions so far?

