01:03:19,836 --> 01:03:26,976
ya da bunların cevaplarını verirken nelere dikkat etmemiz gerektiği, ne gibi stratejiler izleyebileceğimiz çok fazla bize anlatılmıyor.

627
01:03:26,976 --> 01:03:32,856
O yüzden biz bu döneme bunlardan bahsederek girmek istedik ve faydalı olacağını düşünüyoruz.

628
01:03:32,856 --> 01:03:38,496
Okay, to talk about reading comprehension question types.

629
01:03:39,675 --> 01:03:47,336
Generally, we can classify the different question types into two broad categories.

630
01:03:48,256 --> 01:03:57,316
Big picture questions based on the whole passage and specific purpose questions based on some specific elements or parts of the passage.

631
01:03:57,316 --> 01:04:14,115
So, as you can guess, the big picture questions are generally asked in main idea question form, primary purpose question form, or title question form.

632
01:04:14,115 --> 01:04:27,896
So, to be able to answer a main idea question or a primary purpose, the leading purpose, the, how can I say, pioneer purpose question,

633
01:04:28,635 --> 01:04:38,876
the main concern, the main idea, the gist of the passage questions, you need to look at the big picture.

634
01:04:38,876 --> 01:04:43,516
You need to understand the general idea given in the text, okay?

635
01:04:44,296 --> 01:04:46,195
And title questions as well.

636
01:04:46,296 --> 01:04:49,996
Sometimes you read a text without a title and a question asks you,

637
01:04:50,856 --> 01:04:55,476
which of the following titles is the best title for this text?

638
01:04:55,836 --> 01:05:03,796
So, to be able to write a title for the text, you need to read it in detail and you need to understand the general idea given it.

639
01:05:03,796 --> 01:05:08,756
So, I'm going to get into some detail about these question types.

640
01:05:09,836 --> 01:05:15,376
Main idea questions, as you can understand, relate to the central idea or the theme of the passage.

641
01:05:15,735 --> 01:05:18,655
And you're familiar with the question types, I guess.

642
01:05:18,896 --> 01:05:22,155
Which of the following most accurately states the main idea of the passage?

643
01:05:22,316 --> 01:05:25,316
Which of the following best states the central idea of the passage?

644
01:05:25,716 --> 01:05:29,776
The main idea of the passage, the main concern of the author is blah, blah, blah.

645
01:05:29,776 --> 01:05:37,675
As you can see here, which of the following questions are multiple choice questions, right?

646
01:05:38,115 --> 01:05:42,796
Böyle which of the following diye başlayan sorunun çoktan seçmeli bir soru olduğunu anlayabilirsiniz.

647
01:05:43,336 --> 01:05:50,876
Ama bu dönem özellikle de online eğitimde bizim daha ziyade kullanacağımız bu tip cümle tamamlama ya da açık uçlu sorular.

648
01:05:50,996 --> 01:05:54,536
The main idea of the passage is, the main concern of the author is.

649
01:05:54,536 --> 01:05:59,135
Dolayısıyla sizin yazmanız gerekecek main idea'ları çoğu durumda.

650
01:05:59,916 --> 01:06:04,776
Hani çoktan seçmeli bir soruda bunu belirlemek çok daha kolay olabiliyor.

651
01:06:05,235 --> 01:06:11,675
Orada zaten iyi ifade edilmiş bir main idea oluyor ve onları diğerlerinin arasından seçip belirlemek çok daha kolay olabiliyor.

652
01:06:11,756 --> 01:06:13,896
Ama kendiniz yazmanız zor bir şey olabilir.

653
01:06:14,336 --> 01:06:17,936
Ama bu beceriyi kazanmanız gerekiyor ki summarizing yapabilirsiniz.

654
01:06:19,123 --> 01:06:26,143
What's the main concern of the author ya da text gibi bir soru da sizden aslında main idea soruyordur.

655
01:06:26,243 --> 01:06:30,903
Yani farklı şekillerde karşınıza çıksa bile bunların hepsi main idea sorusudur.

656
01:06:31,663 --> 01:06:36,723
So what strategies can I use to be able to answer the main idea questions?

657
01:06:37,423 --> 01:06:43,423
In the answers, look for one or two sentences that are mini summaries of the whole paragraph or passage.

658
01:06:43,563 --> 01:06:46,463
Now we're talking about multiple choice questions here, right?

659
01:06:46,463 --> 01:06:52,343
Look for one or two sentences that are mini summaries of the whole paragraph or passage.

660
01:06:52,843 --> 01:07:00,023
If you find mostly reasons or explanations, the main idea will deal with why, the question why.

661
01:07:00,943 --> 01:07:07,783
I mean, if it's a text written about the reasons of something or the explanations of an issue,

662
01:07:08,143 --> 01:07:11,783
so the main idea will probably deal with the why question.

663
01:07:11,783 --> 01:07:18,983
And if most of the sentences give steps to do or make something, if it's a process writing,

664
01:07:19,263 --> 01:07:22,083
the main idea will deal with how question.

665
01:07:22,223 --> 01:07:27,463
So your answer to the main idea question should answer the question how.

666
01:07:28,263 --> 01:07:33,963
If most of the sentences are about one person or several people or even a group of people,

667
01:07:33,963 --> 01:07:36,884
the main idea will deal with who.

668
01:07:38,283 --> 01:07:41,384
So make sure your choice is not too narrow.

669
01:07:41,603 --> 01:07:45,503
Please keep in mind the main idea question is a big picture question.

670
01:07:45,503 --> 01:07:47,763
So it doesn't deal with details.

671
01:07:48,223 --> 01:07:53,263
It doesn't deal with examples or further explanations.

672
01:07:53,263 --> 01:07:55,983
It deals with the big picture.

673
01:07:56,543 --> 01:08:02,683
So your choice in a multiple choice question shouldn't be too narrow because it's the main,

674
01:08:02,823 --> 01:08:05,083
the central idea of the text.

675
01:08:09,163 --> 01:08:13,143
Make sure your choice for the main idea is not too broad.

676
01:08:13,143 --> 01:08:24,344
This is also wrong because if your main idea includes more things not given in the paragraph or passage,

677
01:08:24,344 --> 01:08:26,963
then it's not specific enough.

678
01:08:26,963 --> 01:08:32,903
Sometimes you might be affected by your own ideas.

679
01:08:32,903 --> 01:08:38,583
But if the question is about the main idea of a text,

680
01:08:39,023 --> 01:08:46,903
your own reasoning, your own ideas, your own background information shouldn't come to the fore.

681
01:08:47,163 --> 01:08:47,463
Okay.

682
01:08:47,983 --> 01:08:54,003
Because we're talking about the text where we have a material at hand and we're dealing with the main idea of it,

683
01:08:54,083 --> 01:08:55,523
not our own opinions.

684
01:08:55,884 --> 01:08:57,583
Our opinions come to the fore.

685
01:08:57,583 --> 01:09:04,403
Our opinions come to the fore when the question asks you to understand something from the text,

686
01:09:04,983 --> 01:09:08,443
infer an information, a piece of information from the text.

687
01:09:09,703 --> 01:09:11,344
Primary purpose questions.

688
01:09:11,603 --> 01:09:15,884
Again, this is another type of big picture question.

689
01:09:16,844 --> 01:09:19,463
The primary purpose of this passage is to.

690
01:09:19,463 --> 01:09:20,644
Okay.

691
01:09:20,644 --> 01:09:29,463
So a passage might aim to give information on a specific subject.

692
01:09:29,684 --> 01:09:32,583
So we call these texts informative texts.

693
01:09:32,884 --> 01:09:33,043
Okay.

694
01:09:33,283 --> 01:09:35,203
So when you are asked such a question,

695
01:09:35,304 --> 01:09:41,663
the primary purpose of this passage is to inform the reader on digital activism, whatever.

696
01:09:42,063 --> 01:09:42,243
Okay.

697
01:09:42,243 --> 01:09:51,563
So here, if you see a question type like this, you should understand, you should remember the purposes of the text.

698
01:09:51,743 --> 01:09:51,923
Okay.

699
01:09:52,103 --> 01:09:55,703
Does it aim to inform the reader?

700
01:09:56,083 --> 01:10:01,543
Does it aim to convince the reader, persuade the reader?

701
01:10:02,583 --> 01:10:06,563
Does it aim to provoke the reader?

702
01:10:06,844 --> 01:10:09,304
For example, provoke the thoughts of the reader.

703
01:10:09,563 --> 01:10:09,844
Okay.

704
01:10:09,844 --> 01:10:15,623
Does it only aim to present opinions, but nothing else?

705
01:10:15,943 --> 01:10:16,203
Okay.

706
01:10:18,323 --> 01:10:22,443
Or does it aim to present solutions to a problem, for example?

707
01:10:22,443 --> 01:10:33,903
The writer sometimes talks about a problem and the writer gives some solutions in his or her writing.

708
01:10:34,543 --> 01:10:42,763
So like with main idea questions, when dealing with purpose questions, you should consider the big picture and the central idea.

709
01:10:44,583 --> 01:10:47,703
And the different question types might be like this.

710
01:10:47,703 --> 01:10:50,963
Which of the following can be the primary focus of this passage?

711
01:10:50,963 --> 01:10:53,844
The main concern of the passage is to.

712
01:10:54,403 --> 01:10:58,423
In the passage, the author is primarily interested in blah, blah, blah.

713
01:10:58,743 --> 01:11:01,723
The passage is chiefly concerned with blah, blah, blah.

714
01:11:02,143 --> 01:11:10,303
But sometimes, please remember, sometimes these main idea questions might not cover the whole text, but it might be only about one paragraph.

715
01:11:10,483 --> 01:11:12,203
So we can ask you this question.

716
01:11:12,303 --> 01:11:14,423
What is the main idea of paragraph three?

717
01:11:14,423 --> 01:11:15,243
Okay.

718
01:11:15,243 --> 01:11:23,683
So then you will only go to paragraph three and you only try to understand the main idea, the central idea of paragraph three, but not the whole text.

719
01:11:23,884 --> 01:11:24,063
Okay.

720
01:11:24,203 --> 01:11:33,003
So sometimes the main ideas, the central issues of the paragraphs might be different from the whole general idea.

721
01:11:33,403 --> 01:11:33,643
Okay.

722
01:11:33,643 --> 01:11:36,043
So this is important.

723
01:11:36,643 --> 01:11:37,683
And title question.

724
01:11:38,683 --> 01:11:45,943
The most appropriate or suitable title for the passage is, which of the following could be the most suitable title for the passage?

725
01:11:46,463 --> 01:11:50,763
So these, when you see these types of questions, you should understand it's a title question.

726
01:11:50,763 --> 01:11:56,523
And it's again, it should again lead you to see the big picture.

727
01:11:58,423 --> 01:11:59,863
What about the specific questions?

728
01:11:59,983 --> 01:12:01,103
Buraya kadar soru var mı?

729
01:12:01,363 --> 01:12:04,463
Big picture soruları dediğimiz sorularla ilgili.

730
01:12:04,983 --> 01:12:10,743
Ana fikir soruları, başlık soruları, metnin birinci amacı nedir soruları.

731
01:12:11,023 --> 01:12:12,983
Hep big picture soruları.

732
01:12:12,983 --> 01:12:19,503
Yani büyük resmi görmekle alakalı, metnin genel fikrini genel olarak ortaya koyduğu fikri anlamakla alakalı.

733
01:12:19,803 --> 01:12:22,003
Bunu anlamadan çözemeyeceğimiz sorular.

734
01:12:22,643 --> 01:12:26,163
O yüzden de şöyle bir göz gezdirip çözebileceğimiz sorular değil.

735
01:12:26,943 --> 01:12:31,623
Ya da sadece bir paragrafa gidip iki üç satır okuyup çözebileceğimiz sorular değil.

736
01:12:32,403 --> 01:12:41,884
Dediğim gibi bütün metni okumanın, bütün metni detaylı satır satır okumanın ve tamamını anlamanın işin içine girdiği soru tipleri bunlar.

737
01:12:41,884 --> 01:12:43,663
Buraya kadar bir soru var mı?

738
01:12:45,643 --> 01:12:46,344
Hayır hocam.

739
01:12:46,563 --> 01:12:47,523
Yani anlaşılırdı.

740
01:12:47,803 --> 01:12:48,583
Ama varsa arkadaşlar.

741
01:12:49,763 --> 01:12:50,103
Okay.

742
01:12:53,103 --> 01:12:54,863
Specific questions'a dönelim.

743
01:12:54,863 --> 01:13:01,063
Fact-based, specific detail or target questions.

744
01:13:01,783 --> 01:13:14,083
Inference questions, paraphrase questions, vocabulary questions, reference questions, and the attitude of the author, the tone of the passage questions are called specific questions.

745
01:13:14,083 --> 01:13:20,023
Now, what are we talking about when we say fact-based or specific detail or target question?

746
01:13:20,443 --> 01:13:25,023
These questions intend to ask you to identify the correct or incorrect facts.

747
01:13:26,063 --> 01:13:27,703
True or false questions, for example.

748
01:13:28,043 --> 01:13:34,823
Or questions starting with according to the passage.

749
01:13:34,923 --> 01:13:37,523
Which of the following is not true according to the text?

750
01:13:37,523 --> 01:13:42,203
In the passage four, or in paragraph four, it is stated that.

751
01:13:42,703 --> 01:13:45,844
So these are, as you can understand, right there questions.

752
01:13:46,023 --> 01:13:54,083
It asks you, these questions ask you to go to the certain part, go to a certain part of the text, find information and write it.

753
01:13:54,203 --> 01:13:54,363
Okay.

754
01:13:54,743 --> 01:13:56,603
Which of the following is not correct?

755
01:13:56,723 --> 01:13:58,183
Which of the following is true?

756
01:13:58,543 --> 01:14:00,123
Which of the following is false?

757
01:14:01,643 --> 01:14:03,304
By blah, blah, blah.

758
01:14:03,304 --> 01:14:05,304
For example, a sentence...

759
01:14:05,492 --> 01:14:23,712
The text is taken and written here by blah, blah, blah. By this sentence, the author means that. What does the writer mean by a word might be given here? A word might be written from the text here. So these are all specific detail or target questions.

760
01:14:23,712 --> 01:14:43,532
Inference questions, as I said, they are indirect conclusions of the passage. In other words, they are not directly stated in the passage. This is where you must draw your own conclusions through a fusion, a combination of what you know and what the author gives.

761
01:14:43,532 --> 01:14:58,952
So this question type can be constructed from a specific paragraph or the whole passage again. So it can be inferred from the text, might be a question type, or it can be inferred from paragraph three, might be a question type.

762
01:14:58,952 --> 01:15:09,992
So if you're talking about only one paragraph, you only go to that paragraph and try to draw conclusions from the information given in that paragraph.

763
01:15:09,992 --> 01:15:28,452
So question types look like this. One can understand from this paragraph. One can figure out from this paragraph. One can conclude from this paragraph or passage that which of the following is more likely to happen according to paragraph three.

764
01:15:28,452 --> 01:15:44,492
Some situations might be given to you in the options and you might be asked which of which of them are likely to happen. It can be inferred. It can be concluded from the passage or it cannot be inferred from the passage.

765
01:15:44,492 --> 01:15:53,512
Bu çıkarım yapılamaz diye de soru sorulabilir. Hangi çıkarım yapılabilir? Hangi çıkarım yapılamaz? Pasajda verilen bilgiler doğrultusunda gibi.

766
01:15:53,512 --> 01:16:12,612
The example blah, blah, blah in paragraph is used to show that. Sometimes some examples, for example, historical examples are given in text and some question types might ask you to find the purpose of this example.

767
01:16:12,612 --> 01:16:23,492
Why does the author give this example? What's its purpose? The sentence blah, blah in the text implies that according to passage,

768
01:16:23,512 --> 01:16:37,612
which of the following must be true or false? Is true or false? No, must be true or false. Okay? If it's is true, is false, it's a specific purpose question or targets, a fact-based question.

769
01:16:37,612 --> 01:16:48,012
But in inference question you see must be. Which of the following must be true? Which of the following would the author agree or disagree with?

770
01:16:48,012 --> 01:17:08,931
Bir yazarın belli bir tonu oluyor genellikle yazı yazarken ve kendi fikirlerini anlattığı bir tekst ise eğer bu, sizin o teksti okuyup size verilen şıklardan hangisiyle o yazarın hemfikir olabileceğini ya da zıt fikirler taşıyabileceğini anlamanız istenebilir bağlı soru tiplerinde.

771
01:17:08,931 --> 01:17:13,971
Aşağıdakilerden hangisiyle bu makalenin yazarı hemfikir olabilir sizce gibi.

772
01:17:14,712 --> 01:17:26,032
Şeyi anlıyorsunuz zannediyorum yani inference questionları cevaplarken, inference sorularını cevaplarken çıkarım yapabilmek için tekste size verilen bilgiyle kendi muhakemenizi birleştiriyorsunuz.

773
01:17:26,132 --> 01:17:32,452
O yüzden tekst tek başına değil, siz tek başınıza değilsiniz. İkisinin bir kombinasyonundan bahsediyoruz.

774
01:17:32,931 --> 01:17:36,512
Paraphrase question. Biraz önce paraphrasingin ne olduğunu söyledim.

775
01:17:37,076 --> 01:17:43,576
Paraphrasing is expressing the same message in different words or rewording for the purpose of clarification.

776
01:17:43,916 --> 01:17:45,136
So it's called restatement.

777
01:17:45,796 --> 01:17:51,916
These questions essentially ask you to explain the meaning of a particular statement in your own words.

778
01:17:51,916 --> 01:17:55,036
This is the most important part that should be underlined.

779
01:17:55,576 --> 01:17:58,876
You report what a person says.

780
01:17:59,216 --> 01:18:05,676
You reword, you restate an author's sentences or ideas in your own words.

781
01:18:07,076 --> 01:18:13,115
The following extract, blah, blah, can be paraphrased as, can be rewritten or restated as.

782
01:18:13,996 --> 01:18:18,975
When you see these structures, you can understand that it's a paraphrase question.

783
01:18:19,336 --> 01:18:25,956
Here, what the author gives you, again, provides a ground for you to make a paraphrase.

784
01:18:26,055 --> 01:18:35,416
But when you try to paraphrase something, you need to call your background information, not your opinions, but this time your grammar.

785
01:18:37,076 --> 01:18:39,416
Knowledge, vocabulary knowledge.

786
01:18:39,695 --> 01:18:39,876
Okay.

787
01:18:40,256 --> 01:18:51,555
So when, when we study paraphrasing, which we will be, which we will start maybe two weeks later, we will start studying paraphrasing.

788
01:18:52,216 --> 01:19:01,096
You will need to remember most of the grammar structures and vocabulary knowledge you learned before.

789
01:19:01,096 --> 01:19:03,655
Vocabulary questions.

790
01:19:03,815 --> 01:19:12,895
Again, sometimes we give certain vocabulary items in bold or in italics in a text and we ask the meanings of the words.

791
01:19:13,435 --> 01:19:22,176
If a question asks you the meaning of a word, it generally includes, the text generally includes clues about the word's meaning.

792
01:19:22,176 --> 01:19:32,336
So when you go to a text, find a word, if it's, if it's a word that you don't know the meaning of, then you should search for the paragraph.

793
01:19:32,336 --> 01:19:41,036
You should look for the previous sentence, the following sentence to be able to guess the meaning, to be able to understand or figure out the meaning of the vocabulary item.

